+    "exported_at": "2026-08-30T19:20:52Z",
+    "body_digest": "sha256:34fa2b991621ee45e0766c4d189da577d13db115c269b85748ad795ec8a5fff5"
+  },
+  "title": "GOV-0090: WP-VAL-A — freeze the badf-release-validation capability contract (G09 independent pre-release validation router; DESIGNED)",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-1, Senior ARCH & ENGIN)** — Plan for WP-VAL-A: freeze the `badf-release-validation` capability contract (G09 independent pre-release validation router; DESIGNED)\n\n## Decision\n\nBuild `badf-release-validation` as the **G09 independent pre-release validation orchestrator** — a risk-routed evidence federation over the four G09 evidence types the lifecycle already names — **not** a G10 release-readiness / go-no-go authority. G09 stays `quality_authority`-owned; G10 stays `release_authority`-owned; that split is untouched.\n\n- **Stage(s):** DEV Glossary stage — governance/validation contract (G09 authoring surface). Stage-Gate 0→1 (contract freeze).\n- **Composes the EXISTING quartet** (confirmed in `badf/lifecycle.json` G09): `quality-validation`, `security-validation`, `performance-test`, `resilience-test`. **No fifth `release-validation` lifecycle evidence type.**\n- **No `scripts/badf_release_validation.py`, no schema, no lifecycle change** at this rung (VAL-I20: no second gate — deterministic G09 semantics live inside the canonical `badf_gate.py` at WP-VAL-C, not a competing validator). WP-VAL-A adds SKILL.md + references only → **ladder-internal, DESIGNED**.\n\n## The model (frozen at this rung)\n\nRoot = a **validation obligation router**: derives the required validation classes (quality / security / performance / resilience) from declared risk, changed surfaces, NFRs, threat model, security obligations and change class — not a static \"run all QA\" checklist. Each class carries its own risk hypothesis, method, **oracle**, execution identity, runtime result and non-coverage. Approved runtimes establish observable facts; agent output is draft until validated and bound. Every artifact binds the **exact** G08-verified candidate (source revision + composed content tree + build/config/env identity + policy epoch). G09 dossier is **conjunctive** (a security blocker cannot be outvoted). Passing one class says nothing about another. Passing G09 establishes pre-release validation evidence — **not** UAT, not operational readiness, not release authority.\n\n## Invariants VAL-I01…VAL-I20 (frozen)\n\nExact candidate (I01) · risk-derived routing (I02) · class independence (I03) · runtime observation (I04) · agent output is draft (I05) · thresholds pre-exist outcomes (I06) · environment provenance (I07) · environment deviation declared (I08) · security-validation ≠ risk acceptance (I09) · performance measurement ≠ conformance (I10) · resilience is hypothesis-driven (I11) · recovery observed (I12) · no class substitution (I13) · blocking findings preserved (I14) · non-coverage mandatory (I15) · flake policy explicit (I16) · G08≠G09 (I17) · G09≠G10 (I18) · G09≠G12 (I19) · no second gate (I20).\n\n## External sources — ADAPT, not authority\n\n`petrkindlmann/qa-skills` → validation-method taxonomy + adapter catalog (risk routing, E2E, accessibility, DB/migration, chaos) — **not** its lifecycle/authority (its `release-readiness` = G10, not G09). Grafana `k6` skills → performance methodology (SLO-backed thresholds, workload classes, generator monitoring). OWASP Secure Agent Playbook → primary security methodology (routes through future `badf-security-assurance`). Individual scanners/runtimes → observation producers, never authority.\n\n## Deliverables (this WP)\n\n`skills/badf-release-validation/SKILL.md` + 17 references (g09-contract, candidate-binding, routing, validation-obligations, class-independence, quality-validation, security-validation, performance-test, resilience-test, runtime-evidence, thresholds-and-oracles, environment-fidelity, findings-and-disposition, noncoverage, g08-g09-g10-boundary, acceptance, external-methodology); `tests/test_badf_release_validation_contract.py` (asserts VAL-I01…I20, the router workflow, composes-existing-quartet, adapt-not-authority, the G08/G09/G10/G12 boundaries, registry DESIGNED); registry entry `badf-release-validation: DESIGNED`; doctrine section.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Registry `badf-release-validation` = DESIGNED; digest = sha256(SKILL.md); no `scripts/badf_release_validation.py`, no schema, no `lifecycle.json` change.\n- Contract test asserts all 20 invariants by id, the obligation-router workflow, \"composes the existing G09 quartet / no fifth type\", \"adapt-not-authority\" for the three external sources, and the G08≠G09≠G10≠G12 boundaries.\n- `repo` clean; CI green on the composed tree.\n\n## Version tier / review\n\nMinor (`0.X.0` — new capability/module, DESIGNED). Ladder-internal (SKILL + references, no gate/schema) → no BADF-QA/BADF-REV review required at A; WP-VAL-B (typed G09 evidence schemas) and WP-VAL-C (deterministic gate controls) are shared-surface → QA+REV by BADF-QA/BADF-REV.\n\nIds: WP-2026-0107 / BADF-DEM-0094 / GOV-0090. Reconciles the land-time-current WP.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T19:20:52Z",
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "note": "WP-VAL-A freezes badf-release-validation as the G09 independent pre-release validation router (DESIGNED): composes the existing G09 quartet, no fifth type, no scripts/badf_release_validation.py/schema/lifecycle change (VAL-I20), VAL-I01..I20, external sources adapt-not-authority. Ladder-internal. DEM-0094/GOV-0090/WP-0107. Reconciles WP-2026-0105."
+}
