+{
+  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
+  "demand_id": "BADF-DEM-0096",
+  "kind": "issue",
+  "source": {
+    "repository": "bstBizEra/badf",
+    "issue": 219,
+    "url": "https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/219",
+    "exported_at": "2026-08-30T20:26:10Z",
+    "body_digest": "sha256:e06c1a43eaf2850c3a1faa48586a1f6afbea8dfe30dab4a17b8d3f0dabcfc3f4"
+  },
+  "title": "GOV-0095: badf-build's frozen contract names a family that does not exist (SKILL.md:31 'badf-verification' → badf-engineering-verification); + the guard, executed as the first real controller run",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-2)** — plan for WP-2026-0109: `badf-build`'s frozen contract names a family that does not exist\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 0 monitor → 1 intake: a measured defect in a shipped artifact; the fix is one line plus the guard that keeps the class out.\n- **Decision:** Continue — the defect is on `main` in an `ACTIVE` family's contract.\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a repo-wide family-name linter for every skill. Refused: the guard is scoped to `skills/badf-build/**`, the surface this work package owns. Other families can adopt it if their own review finds the class.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 7 build (contract accuracy of the build family); nothing later pulled in.\n\n## Observed (measured on `main` `8de88d5`)\n`skills/badf-build/SKILL.md:31`, inside the frozen **Boundary** block, reads:\n\n```text\nbadf-verification (G08)    independently verifies the result\n```\n\n`badf-verification` **is not a family in `badf/skill-registry.json`**. The family that verifies at G08 is `badf-engineering-verification` (BARCHI-3's, `SHADOWED` as of `8de88d5`). Every other family the surface names (`badf-build`, `badf-git`, `badf-implementation-plan`) resolves; this one does not. BARCHI-3 flagged it at their VER-A freeze and left it for this surface's owner rather than editing another seat's contract — correctly.\n\nWhy it matters beyond tidiness: the Boundary block is the part of the contract a build controller reads to know **who verifies its work**. A name that resolves to nothing is a dangling authority reference in an `ACTIVE` family.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0109 / BADF-DEM-0096)\n- `skills/badf-build/SKILL.md`: the Boundary block names `badf-engineering-verification` (G08). No other contract text changes — the twelve stages, BLD-I01…I18 and the fourteen references stay byte-identical.\n- `badf/skill-registry.json`: `badf-build`'s `digest` re-pinned to the new `sha256(SKILL.md)`; `status` `ACTIVE`, `allowed_tools: []`, `risk_class` C1, `source` unchanged. (A skill edited without its registry re-pinned is refused by `repo` — BADF-WP-0032.)\n- `tests/test_badf_build_activation.py`: the frozen-digest literal moves to the new value **and the test's meaning is preserved** — it still asserts `digest == sha256(SKILL.md)`, so a silent edit is still caught.\n- **The guard against the class (failing-first):** a test that every `badf-*` family name appearing anywhere in `skills/badf-build/**` resolves in the registry. Red before the fix, green after.\n- No change to `badf_gate.py`, schemas, the workflow, the references' content, or any other family's files.\n\n## Method — the first real controller run\n`badf-build` is `ACTIVE` (`bbec762`), so this work package is executed **through its own workflow**: `CLAIM → PREFLIGHT → ISOLATE → BASELINE → SLICE → TEST-FIRST → IMPLEMENT → LOCAL VERIFY → SELF-REVIEW → RECONCILE → PACKAGE → HANDOFF`, with the Work Package declaring `expected_surfaces`, `test_obligations` (unit, red required), `execution_budget` and `stop_conditions`, and one slice **delegated** under a narrowed contract.\n\nThat is not extra scope — it is how work is done now. Its by-product is the evidence the BLD-D shadow could not produce: C3 scope containment against a *really declared* surface, C4 red-before-green against a *really declared* obligation, C7 a *real* delegation subset, C6 a declared budget with attempts recorded honestly. #212 (the deferred real-conditions re-shadow) can cite this run as its first real case; discharging #212 itself remains its own later work package.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_every_family_named_in_the_surface_resolves_in_the_registry` (failing-first: `badf-verification` unresolved) · existing activation, contract and shadow pins green.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Any other family's files; the deferred re-shadow (#212); a repo-wide linter.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (defect fix + guard). **Lean mode:** advisory. Review: BADF-QA + BADF-REV (the surface is an `ACTIVE` family's frozen contract).\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T20:26:10Z",
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "note": "badf-build's frozen Boundary block named `badf-verification (G08)`, which resolves to nothing in the registry; the G08 family is badf-engineering-verification. One contract line + registry digest re-pin + the frozen-digest literal + a failing-first guard that every badf-* name in skills/badf-build/** resolves. Executed through badf-build's own workflow -- the first real controller run."
+}
