+{
+  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
+  "demand_id": "BADF-DEM-0097",
+  "kind": "issue",
+  "source": {
+    "repository": "bstBizEra/badf",
+    "issue": 221,
+    "url": "https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/221",
+    "exported_at": "2026-08-30T20:45:30Z",
+    "body_digest": "sha256:c77ac3e54c2b10e9e22d147c874d8f6cdb301296fb61902c47e3df931d0c2bfe"
+  },
+  "title": "GOV-0096: close-out — the G08 ladder's institutional learning (a guard that cannot fail is not a guard) and the five demands it discharges",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-3)** — close-out: the G08 ladder's institutional learning, and the five demands it discharges\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** close-out of the `badf-engineering-verification` program (VER-A…E, landed `e1423ad` → `d292801`).\n- **Decision:** Continue — the ladder is complete and its demands are owed a terminal state with a learning (`BADF-WP-0035`).\n- **Over-engineering risk:** widening this into #220's Tier B fix, or padding five per-rung learnings where the ladder taught one thing. Refused: **one** learning file, **five** demands, no gate/schema change.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 8 engineering verification (close-out); no new stage pulled in.\n\n## Observed (measured on `d292801`)\n\nThe ladder landed A→E and `badf-engineering-verification` is `ACTIVE`. Its five demands — `BADF-DEM-0087 / 0090 / 0092 / 0093 / 0095`, from Issues #195 / #200 / #204 / #207 / #214, **all closed** — were still `AUTHORIZED` and carried no `learning`. Under `BADF-WP-0035` a concluded demand states a `docs/learnings/<slug>.md` or the literal `NONE_DECLARED`; the flip is manual, so it had not happened.\n\nThis is a **five-record subset** of the 87 that #220 measures. It is discharged here because these are this program's own demands and they have a real learning; #220 owns the other 81 and the structural fix, and is deliberately **not** absorbed (see the ARCHI ruling there — no bulk `NONE_DECLARED`).\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0110 / BADF-DEM-0097)\n\n- **`docs/learnings/a-guard-that-cannot-fail-is-not-a-guard.md`** — the ladder's one substantive learning. Its subject is the defect class that produced *every* defect this program shipped or nearly shipped: a check pointed at a **proxy** for its property rather than the property. Instances recorded across **all four seats**, unqualified — spliced assertions that could not fail, a pipe-swallowed exit code, a stale composition record bound before its content, a claim repeated without measuring, a false zero from a silent `.get()` fallback reached independently by two seats, an acceptance criterion that would have flagged working code, an AST fix that produced a second false positive *while fixing this exact class*, and a guard that is correct and unreachable. The generalization and its two mitigations (assert the property directly; give every guard a positive control that has been seen to fail) are BADF-REV's, credited.\n- **Five demands** `0087 / 0090 / 0092 / 0093 / 0095` → `RESOLVED`, each referencing that file. **Failing-first observed:** flipping them terminal *without* the learning field made `badf_gate.py repo` refuse — `demand BADF-DEM-0087 is RESOLVED but declares no learning` — then green once added. That refusal is the **positive control `verify_demand_learnings` has never had**, and it is the direct evidence for #220's claim that the guard is correct and merely unreachable.\n- **#217 numbered into the VER-E doctrine section**, discharging the carried intent recorded in #217's body (\"on close-out or first legitimate touch\"). BADF-REV has asked for a scoped delta check on that file and will get the SHA.\n- `WP-2026-0110` record + composition record + typed G07 self-dossier; `WP-2026-0108` reconciled; lockfile re-signed. **No** gate, schema, lifecycle or CI change.\n\n## Tests\n\nNo new test module: the enforcement already exists (`verify_demand_learnings`, wired into `repo`) and this WP's evidence is that it was **observed red and then green** on the real records. Existing suites must stay green.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n#220 (the other 81 and the derived-transition fix, Tier B, three bound conditions) · #210 / #211 / #216 / #218 · the deferred re-shadow #217 itself.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (docs + demand records). **Lean mode:** advisory. Ladder-internal; QA + REV by BADF-QA and BADF-REV.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T20:45:30Z",
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "note": "Close-out of the badf-engineering-verification G08 program: one institutional learning (docs/learnings/a-guard-that-cannot-fail-is-not-a-guard.md -- the proxy-vs-property defect class, instances across all four seats, BADF-REV's generalization credited) and the discharge of BADF-DEM-0087/0090/0092/0093/0095 to RESOLVED against it. Failing-first observed: the five flipped terminal without a learning made badf_gate.py repo refuse, which is the positive control verify_demand_learnings has never had and the direct evidence for #220's unreachability claim. Also numbers #217 into the VER-E doctrine section, discharging the carried intent recorded in #217's body. No gate/schema/lifecycle change. #220's Tier B fix and the other 81 demands deliberately NOT absorbed."
+}
